// The spall cone's shape — the field thrown from every body exit a round reaches. Read by
// `src/ballistics/spall_cone.rs`, embedded and parsed once, validated at parse. The law itself
// (strength, profile, shadowing, dose) is design doc §5,
// `.agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md`; this file holds only its shape data.
//
// Every value here is a choice the owner can change by editing this file alone; none is a
// constant of the law. The playtest fork on the half-angle and the axis is recorded in
// `.agents/scratch/playtest-forks/README.md`.
(
    // Half-angle α (degrees) of the cone: the rim where the profile's strength reaches zero.
    // TUNED/provisional, owner 2026-10-12; MEASURED normal-impact outer extents ~26° (Qi et al.
    // 2026, see .agents/scratch/damage-cam-2026-10-08/research/cloud-angle-deep.md).
    half_angle_deg: 25.0,

    // The cone's axis. `RearNormalBisector`: normalize(rear-face outward normal + exit direction)
    // at a genuine exit, the exit direction at an internal step (which has no face).
    // `ExitDirection`: the exit direction everywhere.
    // ENGINEERING ASSUMPTION, MEASURED support Verolme 1997, Recht & Howell 1967 (debris axis about
    // halfway between the shot line and the plate normal; 25° measured against 22.5° predicted at
    // 45° obliquity — research/cloud-angle-deep.md).
    axis: RearNormalBisector,

    // N, the number of directions the cone is sampled by, in equal-solid-angle strata of weight
    // 1/N. Resolution, not balance: the emitted total is S/2 at every N, so N changes how finely a
    // box's dose is resolved, never how much the cone carries.
    directions: 24,
)
